  .brief-card { padding: 13px 14px; }
  .brief-head { padding-bottom: 8px; font-size: 7px; }
  .brief-lede { margin: 9px 0; font-size: 10px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .brief-steps { gap: 6px; }
  .brief-steps li { font-size: 9px; line-height: 1.4; gap: 6px; }
  .brief-threat { margin-top: 9px; padding-top: 8px; font-size: 6.5px; }
  .brief-net { display: none; }
  .modal-card { padding: 20px; }
  .help-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .end-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  .rotate-hint { display: none; }
}
@media (max-width: 390px) {
  .brief-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .brief-card { max-height: 200px; overflow-y: auto; }
  .title-main h1 { font-size: 46px; }
}
@media (max-height: 620px) and (orientation: landscape) {
  .title-topline { display: none; }
  .title-grid { align-items: center; padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 14px; gap: 20px; }
  .title-main h1 { font-size: clamp(44px, 8.5vw, 76px); }
  .tagline { display: none; }
  .start-row { margin-top: 14px; }
  .title-foot { display: none; }
  .brief-card { max-height: 62dvh; overflow-y: auto; }
  .brief-doctrine { display: none; }
  .kicker { margin-bottom: 10px; }
}
@media (max-width: 900px) and (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 560px) {
  .topbar { flex-wrap: nowrap; }
  .trace-cluster { order: 0; width: auto; flex: 1; }
  .trace-top { display: none; }
  .intel-cluster { top: calc(58px + var(--safe-top)); }
  .panel {
    top: 64px; bottom: 10px; left: auto; right: 10px;
    width: min(360px, 48vw);
    max-height: none;
    transform: translateX(16px);
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-line);
    padding: 10px 12px;
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, calc(100% - 12px) 0, 100% 12px, 100% 100%, 12px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 12px));
  }
  .panel.open { transform: none; }
  .coach { bottom: 10px; }
  .breach-grid .cell { min-height: 28px; }
  .freq { height: 42px; }
}

/* Reduced motion */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .scan::after, .freq-scan, .intel-pips i, .scan { animation: none !important; }
  .live-dot, .blink, .threat-dot { animation: none !important; }
}

content.text:
Now the main JS. This is the big one. Let me plan exact code.

Imports:
```js
import * as THREE from '../vendor/three.module.js'
```

DOM helper `$ = id => document.getElementById(id)`.

Constants:
- EARTH_R = 10
- STATION lat 38.9 lon -77 → convert to vec3. Note the visible side camera initial. stationDir = (cos(lat)*sin(lon), sin(lat), cos(lat)*cos(lon)). lon negative → x negative, z positive. camera position = stationDir * dist with yaw/pitch? Set camera yaw = atan2(stationDir.x, stationDir.z), pitch = asin(stationDir.y) maybe. But pitch then 0.68 rad means looking down at the north; station centered. That's fine, but globe tilted. Better camera pitch 0.22 and yaw = atan2(stationDir.x, stationDir.z) so station is near center (slightly south). Let's compute: camera at yaw ang gives direction (sin yaw, tan-ish?). With pitch .2, position = dist*(cosP sinY, sinP, cosP cosY). Station at lat .68. The station is 27° south of camera's equator view. Hmm.

Maybe choose station lat 28° to reduce; still. We can set camera pitch = stationLat*0.7 = 0.35. That views from 20° above equator, station visible near center. Good.

Sun direction: need day side lit. Set sun = normalize(-0.65, 0.4, 0.75)? Camera is around stationDir (x=-0.577? compute lon -77: sin=-0.974, cos=0.225; cosLat=0.78; x=-0.76, y=0.63, z=0.175). Sun at (-0.65,0.4,0.75) would light the left/front. Fine.

Let's define `SUN = new THREE.Vector3(-0.55, 0.35, 0.76).normalize()`.

