To test win quickly, we can automate hook+breach for 4 satellites, which should be feasible. But trace might hit 100 during the first satellite? Trace starts 5, rate ~0.31/s linked. Hook 3 locks each maybe 1s if we tap when in zone; breach 3 layers each ~3-4 glyph taps with DOM re-render. Might take 5-8s per sat, trace ~+3-5 per sat, minus 6 per capture. Counter at 34s. Should be fine.

Automation:
```
async function hookAndBreach(name) {
  await page.locator('.rail-chip', {hasText:name}).click()
  // hook loop: wait for panel, then while breachView hidden:
  for (let i=0;i<200;i++){
    const state = await page.evaluate(() => {
      const breach = !document.getElementById('breachView').hidden
      const needle = parseFloat(document.getElementById('freqNeedle').style.left)
      const zone = document.getElementById('freqZone')
      const zl = parseFloat(zone.style.left), zw = parseFloat(zone.style.width)
      return {breach, needle, zl, zw, lockDisabled: document.getElementById('lockBtn').disabled, secured: !document.getElementById('securedView').hidden, counter: !document.getElementById('counterAlert').hidden}
    })
    if counter purge.
    if state.breach break
    if secured -> done
    if needle within zone -> click lock
    wait 30ms
  }
  // breach loop:
  while breach active:
     read seq = document.querySelectorAll('.proto-cell') text? The seq is shown as proto cells; current cell has class 'current'. To determine next glyph, use `.proto-cell.current` text (not done). Since progress marks done. 
     Then click `.cell[data-glyph="X"]` (first matching). But glyphs might be HTML special chars? Sat symbols likely unicode. Attribute selector could break with quotes; easier use page.evaluate to find button with dataset.glyph === current and click it. But clicking via JS dispatch event? `.click()` should trigger delegated listener on breachGrid. Use `page.evaluate(g => { [...document.querySelectorAll('#breachGrid .cell')].find(b=>b.dataset.glyph===g)?.click() }, glyph)`.
```
Need to handle during breach: protoRow re-render happens instantly after each click. Read next current after small wait.

Actually the sequence has multiple same glyphs; reading `.proto-cell.current` works because renderBreach sets current class at index progress. But after progress>=len, completeLayer renders next layer. So loop reads.

Need to watch counter alert each iteration and click purge.

Potential issue: selecting 4 sats while above. HELIOS/KESTREL captured? We'll choose ARGUS-7, VESPER-2, NOMAD-6, TALON-4 (all above now, elevations 61/39/19/16). During the ~1 min test, they may pass below horizon. LEO satellites speed maybe; elevation changes. NOMAD at 19°, TALON 16°, could set soon. Summary says pass windows are ~a few minutes? Let's check speeds. At 34s counter. Could be okay. Alternatively KESTREL-1 elevation 12°, less. Could use HELIOS at 26.

If sat drops below during hook, lock disabled. We may need to wait for AOS (could be long). To avoid, maybe capture fastest and resilient. But test can also be done by restarting and using first sats.

Let's look at updateWorld satellite angular speed.

